# that fired, and per-stream scope for each cycle, plus the evidence sweep
# result". `measure-run.py` `_read_stream_rollup` walked `bucket.items()`
# treating EVERY key as a stream id and was never taught any of it.
#
# Driven at 056f51a as a real process, against this run's own archive:
#
#   $ python3 plugins/foundry/scripts/measure-run.py foundry-archive/daring-orca
#   EXIT=1
#   failure_tokens: ["PHASE9_SCHEMA_INVALID" x4,
#                    "PHASE9_UNKNOWN_STREAM:stream_scope" x2,
#                    "PHASE9_UNKNOWN_STREAM:evidence_sweep" x2]
#
# Four non-stream keys x cycles 10 and 11 = the eight tokens. Both names are in
# UNREADABLE_ARTIFACT_TOKENS, so `_exit_status` returned 1. The SAME command on
# foundry-archive/thunder-viper — an archive that PREDATES those keys — exited 0
# with no tokens. AC-039's acceptance instrument rejected the current run's
# well-formed artifact and accepted the old one.
#
# The numbers themselves were never wrong: baseline 22/8, current 12/0, target
# 12/3, meets_target true on both axes. NFR-001 says "Numbers are the target,
# not a gate"; what was wrong was the VERDICT asserted about the document.
#
# At this commit, the same two drives (they cannot be the evidence command
# itself — /foundry-archive/ is git-ignored, so it does not exist in the
# detached worktree the sweep re-executes in):
#
#   $ python3 plugins/foundry/scripts/measure-run.py foundry-archive/daring-orca
#   EXIT=0   failure_tokens: []   cycles: 12
#   coverage now read for all twelve cycles 0-11 (it stopped at nine before)
#   $ python3 plugins/foundry/scripts/measure-run.py foundry-archive/thunder-viper
#   EXIT=0   failure_tokens: []   cycles: 22        (unchanged)
#
# THE FIX IS ONE DEFINITION, NOT A THIRD COPY. Three modules walk this bucket.
# Two had grown the rule by hand (`foundry_orchestrator._stream_dispatch_cycles`,
# `foundry_report._read_dispatch_summary`) and the third had not — which is what
# two hand-typed copies of one rule cost. The rule is now stated once as
# `foundry_state.is_stream_record`, in the leaf module all three already import,
# for the same reason and at the same address as `unreported_dispatch_pairs`
# (D-047 / D-048). The two walkers casting 5 owns READ it; casting 3's copy is
# pinned behaviourally by a test that feeds one bucket to both readers, and the
# recommendation to adopt it is in concerns.md.
#
# NOT A DENYLIST OF KEY NAMES. The filing names four keys; there are five
# (`temper_entry`, the nested sub-bucket the F5 entry writes under), and the next
# C-6 field would be a sixth. The test is on the VALUE: a tranche is exactly a
# mapping carrying `records`, because `_record_stream_rollup` appends to
# `entry["records"]` on every mark and no cycle-level fact has that key.
#
# AND THE ONE FAULT THAT IS STILL A FAULT. Filtering by value ALONE would have
# traded the false alarm for a new silence: `prove` holding a string is a BROKEN
# stream record, not a cycle-level fact. The key is resolved against the roster
# before the value test decides, so a roster key with a non-tranche value stays
# PHASE9_SCHEMA_INVALID — pinned by
# test_a_roster_key_whose_value_is_not_a_tranche_is_still_a_fault.
#

